# Regression tests that airos-ci runs inside every image its smoke test boots
# in QEMU (airos-ci images/build-image.sh builds them with the image,
# images/smoke-test.sh copies them in and runs them at boot through
# ~/config/settings/boot/UserBootscript, with their output on the serial log).
#
# One jam target per line: a test program (SimpleTest) that prints what it
# checked and exits with 0 when everything passed. A test must end by itself
# within a minute, also when the bug it guards against is back: give every
# wait a deadline.

# _kern_block_thread() and signals: an interrupted user wait spun forever
# (hung Deskbar menu, kernel fix bcd3806fd1)
user_block_thread_test
# the same through libroot's rw_lock (BLooperList's lock)
rw_lock_signal_test
# a device behind a full speed hub (QEMU usb-hub) enumerates: xHCI built its
# route string from the transaction translator's port
usb_hub_child_test
# pipe() with a full FD table waited forever for a reader instead of failing
# with EMFILE; a failed FIFO open left its writer count behind (haiku#59)
pipe_fd_table_full_test
# vfork() + exec while other threads allocate: a child forked while another
# thread held a heap lock never got it (net_server's service launch hung)
vfork_malloc_test
